---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { links } from '../config';
const scenes = [
  ['morning', 'Morning', '05:00–09:59'],
  ['day', 'Day', '10:00–15:59'],
  ['evening', 'Evening', '16:00–18:59'],
  ['night', 'Night', '19:00–04:59'],
];
---
<Base title="Village wallpaper" description="Try a free 3840×2400 village wallpaper for macOS, with morning, day, evening and night scenes. Optional support through Saweria.">
  <div class="wrap page">
    <div class="narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Free download · Dynamic HEIC preview</p>
      <h1>A village for every<br />part of your day.</h1>
      <p>Bring a little of the MacDigiPet village to your desktop while the app grows. Four lighting scenes follow your Mac’s local time, from a quiet morning to lantern-lit night.</p>
      <p class="muted">3840 × 2400 · 16:10 · HEIC · 24.0 MiB · No app required</p>
      <div class="row actions"><a class="btn" href="/downloads/macdigipet-village-v4-dynamic.heic" download>Download free wallpaper</a><a class="btn" href={links.kofi} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="heart" aria-hidden="true">♥</span>Support on Ko-fi</a><a class="btn" href={links.saweria} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span class="heart" aria-hidden="true">♥</span>Support on Saweria</a></div>
      <p class="muted">The download is free. Tips are optional and support development time and tools.</p>
      <p class="muted">For personal, non-commercial wallpaper use. Read the <a href="/license#personal-wallpaper-use">Copyright &amp; License</a> terms.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid wallpaper-preview">
      {scenes.map(([phase, name, time]) => <figure class="shot"><img src={`/img/wallpaper-${phase}.jpg`} alt={`Village in ${name.toLowerCase()} light`} width="960" height="600" loading="lazy" /><figcaption><strong>{name}</strong> · {time} local time</figcaption></figure>)}
    </div>
    <div class="narrow">
      <h2>Set it up on your Mac</h2>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li>Download the HEIC file and keep it somewhere on your Mac.</li>
        <li>Open <strong>System Settings → Wallpaper</strong> and add the downloaded image. The wording varies between macOS versions.</li>
        <li>Select <strong>Dynamic</strong> if macOS offers that appearance option. Your Mac controls when the picture refreshes.</li>
      </ol>
      <div class="notice"><strong>Preview compatibility:</strong> All four images and the time metadata have passed file checks. Automatic switching in macOS Wallpaper settings is still awaiting real-device testing. If it stays on one scene, please share your macOS version in <a href={links.discord} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Discord</a>.</div>
      <h2>About the artwork</h2>
      <p>A fan-made village scene inspired by Digimon World 1, created with AI-assisted imagery and upscaled to 4K. There are no characters baked into the wallpaper. It is not an official Bandai or Toei release.</p>
      <p class="checksum">SHA-256: 4569c0aaf38641e947ccf57239f6057c2b996f2a29670f55a1289d79f3673248</p>
      <h2>Meet your future desktop partner</h2>
      <p>The wallpaper is a first taste of the village. <a href={links.discord} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Join Discord</a> to follow the companion app, share your desktop and swap ideas. Everyone is welcome, with no need to sign up for testing.</p>
      <p>The first beta is being prepared for testers in Discord. No release date has been set. If you’d like to help test, <a href="/beta">see how the beta works</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
